Scope note for this repository

This licence applies to the toolkit source, its documentation and the
toolkit-authored payload. The `document-corpus-bridge` topic skill bundle is
toolkit-authored and is covered by it directly.

The `theological-research` topic skill bundle is the work of s. Denisa and
Michal, staged into the toolkit from their working copy. It is also under the
MIT licence, but under its own copyright line: the bundle carries its own
`LICENSE` file (`Copyright (c) 2026 s. Denisa + Michael`) inside
`extension/bundles/theological-research/`, and that file, not this one, is the
licence that travels with the installed skill. Both bundles are therefore
publishable. See
`docs/implementation/phase-9-document-ingestion/bundle-notes.md`.

Neither licence grants rights over anything the toolkit only refers to: the
works a user cites, the Crossref, OpenAlex or Zotero records a user retrieves,
or a licensed database such as ATLA.
